From: AIpath <aidiginext@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 05:12:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix a NameError in the stock search-terms step, and add a
 check that catches it

"Work out the search terms" failed with `name 'ROLE_IMAGE_PROMPT' is not defined`.
The role constant was used but never imported, and no test executed that step, so
46 passing checks said nothing about it.

- import ROLE_IMAGE_PROMPT in the YouTube pipeline
- tests/lint.py runs pyflakes over every file and fails on undefined names,
  shadowed definitions and dead locals, whether the line ever executes or not
- tests/integration.py now actually runs the stock search-terms step
- tidied the findings the new check surfaced: two stray f-prefixes, one unused
  result, and eight dead bindings in the tests themselves
- CI runs the static check before either suite

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
